  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1139 AM MDT Wed Oct 7 2026\n\nISOLATED SHOWERS AND THUNDERSTORMS:\n\nThere has been very little change from the pattern yesterday. In \nfact, models are still showing that weak circulation over our area \nonce again. Expect showers and storms to develop this afternoon \nmainly over the higher terrain. Outflow boundaries moving off the \nterrain will focus additional development over the valleys into the \nevening hours. These storms will be capable of producing small hail, \ngusty winds and localized heavy rainfall. Tomorrow is not much \ndifferent, so expect showers and storms with similar impact. \nTemperatures are running 10-15 degrees above normal, but cool down \ncloser to normal over the weekend.\n\n\nPOTENTIAL FOR MORE WIDESPREAD PRECIPITATION:\n\nThe pattern gets much more complicated this weekend. A low pressure \ndropping southward along the West Coast will steer the remnants of \nHurricane Rachel into the Desert Southwest. As of now models agree \nthe remnants will track over Southern Cal and Las Vegas before \ngetting absorbed into the deepening low pressure. For our are that \nmeans increasing southwest flow and moisture advection beginning on \nSaturday. Therefore precipitation chances and coverage increases. On \nSunday we should get the affects of the remnant tropical system. The \nmain uncertainties are how much forcing and or convection will we \nactually get. There looks to be a break on Monday before a potential \nsecond round, but that could change at this point too. As the low \npressure spins over the Desert Southwest it begins to pull mositure \nnorthward from Mexico. This moisture may also be tropical in nature, \nso we would expect increasing precipitation chances. Eventually the \nlow pressure moves eastward over the region. This second round would \ntake place Tuesday onward. The low pressure would certainly bring \nforcing and a cooler airmass to our area, but these cut off low \npressures are notorious for stalling out longer than the models \ninitially show. Therefore confidence in the details is low attm.",
